# The three variables every signed-in Playwright spec in `frontend/e2e/` reads.
#
# Copy to `.env.e2e` (gitignored by `.env.*`) and fill in a real login. This file is committed and
# the copy is not, which is the same split `.env.example` already uses — the NAMES are repository
# knowledge and the VALUES never are. `.gitignore`'s own banner carries the rest: a line there stops
# the next mistake and does nothing about a secret already on disk, which has to be rotated.
#
# A spec with these unset SKIPS itself and says so. That is deliberate: a developer without a live
# login gets a green run reporting a skip rather than a red one reporting nothing.
#
#   # from frontend/, POSIX:
#   set -a; . ../.env.e2e; set +a
#   npx playwright test e2e/zz-ministry-dashboard-live.spec.ts
#
# ⚠ E2E_BASE_URL must be THIS portal, which is `designer-repository.vercel.app`.
# The field repository is a DIFFERENT product; its alias `field-repository.vercel.app` sits in the
# same Vercel team and shares almost every name with ours, so pointing this at it would run a
# signed-in spec against somebody else's live estate. docs/CI.md §0 is the register of which value
# belongs to which product.
#
# ⚠ Any account used here acts for real on whatever E2E_BASE_URL points at. The specs that read it
# are read-only by construction; a spec that needs to write needs its own account and its own
# decision.

E2E_BASE_URL=https://designer-repository.vercel.app
E2E_EMAIL=
E2E_PASSWORD=
